class.description:
[CSV] converts comma-separated values ([url=https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4180]RFC 4180[/url]) to an [Array] of rows and back, with the same API as [JSON] and [TOML]: [method parse] (with error details), [method parse_string] and [method stringify] for data, [method serialize] and [method deserialize] for resources.
Cells that contain the delimiter, a double quote, a line break or leading or trailing spaces are written in double quotes, and a double quote inside is doubled ([code]""[/code]). The delimiter comes from [member SerializerOptions.csv_delimiter] (one character, for example [code];[/code] or a tab).
With [member SerializerOptions.csv_headers] (the default), the first row names the columns and [method parse] returns an [Array] of [Dictionary], one per row, keyed by column name. Without it, every row is a [PackedStringArray]. Cells are always [String]s, there is no type guessing ([code]007[/code] stays [code]"007"[/code]).
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var csv = CSV.new()
if csv.parse("name,level\nAnn,3\n\"Bob, the 2nd\",7\n") == OK:
	for row in csv.get_data():
		print(row["name"], " ", int(row["level"]))
else:
	print("Line %d: %s" % [csv.get_error_line(), csv.get_error_message()])

print(CSV.stringify([{ "name": "Ann", "level": 3 }]))
# name,level
# Ann,3
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var csv = new Csv();
if (csv.Parse("name,level\nAnn,3\n\"Bob, the 2nd\",7\n") == Error.Ok)
{
	foreach (var row in csv.GetData())
	{
		var record = row.AsGodotDictionary();
		GD.Print(record["name"], " ", record["level"].AsString().ToInt());
	}
}
else
{
	GD.Print($"Line {csv.GetErrorLine()}: {csv.GetErrorMessage()}");
}

var rows = new Godot.Collections.Array { new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "name", "Ann" }, { "level", 3 } } };
GD.Print(Csv.Stringify(rows));
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] The static methods can be called from any thread. A [CSV] instance should be used by one thread at a time.
